From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:25:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0086: a read that cannot fault is issued whatever
 the guest's condition

Kyty checks the guest's bounds in the shader on a device without byte-granular robustBufferAccess2 (RADV
rounds to 4 bytes), and it wrapped every buffer read in a branch: if (in bounds and lane active) read, else
zero. ACO then waited for each read before the next could start (s_waitcnt vmcnt(0) at the merge, where the
other side writes the same register), reloaded its descriptor in every branch, and could not widen
neighbouring reads. A guest s_buffer_load_dwordx4 became four branches, four descriptor loads and four
waits in a row.

A storage buffer descriptor cannot fault: Kyty requires robustBufferAccess and nullDescriptor, a missing
buffer is a null descriptor, and every slot a shader reads is written for each draw. Such a read is now
issued unconditionally and the same condition selects its value or the default (EmitReadOrDefault), so
the guest still reads exactly the same values. Scalar loads, raw and formatted buffer loads of descriptor
buffers take this path; physical addresses (BDA, indirect buffers), LDS, GDS, scratch, atomics, stores and
coherent reads keep their branch. The descriptor index of an indirect buffer stays checked before use.

A vector read issued for every lane would also fetch for the lanes the guest has switched off, at their
stale addresses: in a loop whose lanes leave one by one, that is memory traffic the branch avoided (a
full-screen pixel shader of Astro Bot took 1.12 ms instead of 0.56-0.98 in a first form). While such a
read is emitted, the lanes it reads for are in EmitterState::read_lanes, and ByteAddress sends the others
to UINT32_MAX, past every binding, where the device returns zero without touching memory.

Offline, on the device's RADV (pipeline creation only): Astro Bot's foliage vertex shader goes from
138 descriptor loads, 133 single-dword reads and 121 full memory waits to 16, 35 single-dword reads plus
37 wider ones, and 19 waits; 35 242 such reads in 324 of the garden's 350 modules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
